coding rule","fontSize":24,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","id":"e42"},{"type":"text","x":950,"y":238,"text":"1. shift each logit by the threshold:\n    aᵢ = sᵢ − logit(τ)\n    (aᵢ > 0 exactly when pᵢ > τ)\n2. pick the contiguous range with the\n    largest sum of aᵢ (Kadane, O(K))\n3. its interval boundaries are the\n    answer; if all aᵢ < 0, take the best\n    single interval","fontSize":20,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","id":"e43"},{"type":"text","x":70,"y":615,"text":"shifted logits aᵢ:  -4.0  -3.4  -2.5  +3.3  +5.5  +5.6  +5.7  +5.3  +2.7  +0.4","fontSize":19,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","fontFamily":8,"id":"e44"},{"type":"text","x":70,"y":660,"text":"The last interval (p = 0.33) is still above τ, so the span runs to the end of the clip. τ = 0.25 is fixed for all\nexperiments and both model sizes.","fontSize":20,"strokeColor":"#6b6f76","id":"e45"},{"type":"text","x":70,"y":857.4,"text":"github.com/MCG-NJU/VideoJev README (query: 'The woman in green eats pasta.'); VideoJev (arXiv:2610.18615), Eq. (4)","fontSize":17,"strokeColor":"#6b6f76","id":"e46"},{"type":"text","x":1524.6,"y":856.8,"text":"11","fontSize":18,"strokeColor":"#adb5bd","id":"e47"}]